  "changes": [
    "The native plugin and all original bundled skills are retained. The official SHOPLINE Developer MCP 1.1.0 executable source is included with its own MIT license.",
    "The bundle invokes the fixed local Node entry with structured arguments instead of running an unversioned npx command at every startup. All eleven dependencies actually imported by the complete single-file backend are retained; four unused manifest-only packages are omitted, with the original manifest preserved.",
    "The MCP config and cache use the explicitly supplied DSH_HOME data directory. Missing or non-absolute data paths fail before any backend initialization.",
    "The official Alpha MCP client must complete the initial connection and tool discovery; startup failure cannot be reported as successful MCP activation."
  ],
